<body>
    <h1>Multimedia Practice</h1>
    <p>I kept this page simple on purpose. It just shows I can embed different types of media in valid HTML.</p>

    <h2>Image</h2>
    <figure>
        <img
            src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Firefox_logo%2C_2019.svg"
            alt="Firefox logo"
            width="220"
            height="220">
        <figcaption>Example image (Firefox logo).</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Video</h2>
    <video controls width="520">
        <source src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        Sorry, your browser can’t play this video.
    </video>

    <h2>Audio</h2>
    <audio controls>
        <source src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-audio/t-rex-roar.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
        Sorry, your browser can’t play this audio.
    </audio>

    <h2>Embedded page</h2>
    <iframe
        src="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/"
        title="MDN Web Docs"
        width="700"
        height="350"
        loading="lazy">
    </iframe>

    <p><a href="../part2-planet-table/planets.html">Go to Part 2 (Tables)</a></p>
</body>
